   116	
   117	    a_12 a_23 a_31 = a_21 a_32 a_13.
   118	
   119	Indeed, multiply the three equations d_i a_ij=d_j a_ji around the cycle and cancel d_1 d_2 d_3. Conversely, this condition permits construction of consistent diagonal entries by ratios along two edges. The respective absolute cycle products for the three matrices are 2 versus 1, 1 versus 8, and 8 versus 18. Hence all three are genuinely nonsymmetrizable, not rank-two or tree-shaped instances already covered by symmetrization.
