   143	    ad(f_j1) ... ad(f_jm) f_i,   all j_k in J,
   144	
   145	with exactly alpha_j occurrences of each index j in J. This spanning statement follows from Jacobi: a negative bracket word containing exactly one f_i can be rewritten with that f_i innermost and all other factors acting on it.
   146	
   147	Move these adjoint operators across the invariant pairing. Up to a sign, the result is a pairing of f_i with a composition of J-lowerings applied to x. All intermediate vectors stay in W, and the final degree is epsilon_i, whose W component is zero. Hence x pairs to zero with the whole opposite root space. Nondegeneracy gives x=0. Thus W=0 in the slice, proving I_alpha=K_alpha. QED.
