   149	**Rank-three corollary.** Every rank-two GCM is symmetrizable: for [[2,-p],[-r,2]] with p,r>0, diag(r,p) is a symmetrizer; the disconnected case is immediate. Therefore for every rank-three GCM, equality holds at every degree having a zero or one coordinate. Any additional positive relation must have all three coordinates at least two. In particular the entire height-at-most-five range is excluded uniformly, and (2,2,2) at height six is the first possible full-support degree. This is much stronger than a finite sample but still leaves infinitely many interior degrees.
