   151	The proof does not assume that a singular rank-two Cartan matrix has independent rows. If using the alternative lowest-weight-module proof, a full Levi Cartan realization must be chosen inside the ambient full realization. The comparison proof above avoids that extra representation-theoretic bookkeeping.
   152	
   153	## 8. Necessary condition on a first extra relation
   154	
   155	Suppose the extra ideal tau/I is nonzero, and choose a nonzero homogeneous element x of least positive height. Then every D_i x is zero, by minimality. In the Serre quotient the adjoint actions of e_i and f_i are locally nilpotent: this holds on each Chevalley/Cartan generator by the Serre relations and the sl2 relations, and hence on every finite bracket by the iterated derivation rule. The sl2-submodule generated by the lowest-weight vector x is therefore finite-dimensional. Its lowest h_i-weight is a nonpositive integer. Consequently
   156	
   157	    sum_j a_ij alpha_j <= 0 for every i.
   158	
   159	For a rank-three counterexample, combine this with Section 7: a first extra relation can only occur at an interior degree alpha_j>=2 in the fundamental imaginary cone A alpha<=0. This is a necessary condition, not an existence result. The computed examples include such interior degrees rather than testing only the already-excluded boundary.
   160	
   161	## 9. Remaining mathematical gap
   162	
   163	Agreement at finite height does not imply I=K in all heights. The recurrence constructs an exact search for a first additional relation, but supplies no uniform bound on where a first relation would occur if one exists. A proof of the book conjecture requires an all-height argument for every nonsymmetrizable GCM, not three matrices and not a finite-dimensional truncation. Conversely a modular discrepancy needs exact characteristic-zero confirmation and explicit witness verification before it can be called a counterexample.

