    69	### Exact algorithm and proof of its meaning
    70	
    71	[`proof.md`](proof.md) proves, without assuming the conjecture, that the positive maximal ideal is obtained recursively by
    72	
    73	    K_ei=0,
    74	    K_alpha={x in L_alpha : D_i x in K_(alpha-ei) for all i}.
    75	
    76	It also proves the exact Serre-ideal recurrence from the original generators plus [e_i,I_(alpha-ei)]. Thus dim L_alpha/I_alpha and dim L_alpha/K_alpha are genuinely different constructions being compared, not two labels for one quotient. The code does not use a symmetrizable root-multiplicity formula for a nonsymmetrizable input.
    77	
    78	The producer, [`work/graded_lie.py`](work/graded_lie.py), uses recursive bracket lowering. The separate checker, [`work/check_certificate.py`](work/check_certificate.py), imports no producer code and computes lowering by an independently derived associative-word deletion formula, followed by independently reconstructed coordinates. It regenerates exact Serre spans and checks injectivity on their quotients, which proves I=K inductively; a nonzero-defect certificate is explicitly refused rather than mislabeled an equality pass. The height, matrix set, and entries are bound to an external requested scope and fixed specification. Six negative controls test field, missing degree, changed dimension, omitted matrix, altered matrix, and height. A finite-field rank match alone is not the accepted evidence; the exact-Q certificate and independent checker are the acceptance path.
    79	
    80	### Proved infinite boundary family
    81	
    82	**If deleting one index i leaves a symmetrizable principal GCM, then I_alpha=K_alpha in every degree with alpha_i=1.** The proof constructs a symmetrizable comparison matrix preserving the entire coefficient-one Serre slice and every complementary lowering, then uses its nondegenerate opposite-root pairing. It does not assume the full nonsymmetrizable algebra has an invariant symmetric form.
    83	
    84	For rank three this excludes **every** degree with a zero or one coordinate, at all heights. In particular equality holds uniformly through height five for every rank-three GCM. The first unexcluded full-support degree is (2,2,2), not (2,2,1). An independently derived all-(m,1,1) calculation and the full comparison proof are preserved in [`evidence/descent-audit.md`](evidence/descent-audit.md). These are consequences of known symmetrizable theory; novelty has not been established.
    85	
    86	A first extra relation must also be annihilated by every lowering. Integrable sl2 theory then gives the necessary condition A alpha<=0. This directs the remaining attack to interior imaginary degrees, not already-excluded boundary degrees.
    87	
    88	### Bounded exact computations
    89	
    90	The three genuinely nonsymmetrizable input matrices are
    91	
    92	    A_one   = [[2,-1,-1],[-1,2,-1],[-2,-1,2]],
    93	    A_cycle = [[2,-1,-2],[-2,2,-1],[-1,-2,2]],
    94	    A_large = [[2,-2,-2],[-3,2,-2],[-2,-3,2]].
    95	
    96	Their absolute directed cycle products are respectively 2 vs 1, 1 vs 8, and 8 vs 18, excluding a diagonal symmetrizer.
    97	
    98	The exact-Q producer found **no discrepancy in any positive multidegree through height 10** for all three and for the A3 / affine-A2 controls: 258 nonzero free-Lie degrees per matrix. It also found no discrepancy through height 12 for A_one: 421 nonzero free-Lie degrees. All other positive degrees in those ranges have zero free-Lie dimension. These are bounded computations, not the full theorem.
    99	
   100	| Matrix | dim at (2,2,2), both quotients | dim at (3,3,3), both quotients |
   101	|---|---:|---:|
   102	| A_one | 3 | 8 |
   103	| A_cycle | 5 | 31 |
   104	| A_large | 14 | 148 |
   105	| affine-A2 control | 2 | 2 |
   106	
   107	The free-Lie dimensions at those degrees are 14 and 186. The samples include interior weights in A alpha<=0, so the computation is not just rechecking the boundary theorem. Evidence: [`evidence/interior-root-samples.json`](evidence/interior-root-samples.json), full producer certificates/results under `evidence/rational-height10/` and `evidence/rational-height12/`. Independent-check receipts, when present, are the separate verification authority; a producer result is not silently treated as an independent pass.
   108	
   109	### Symbolic interior attempt and limits
   110	
   111	`work/interior_minor.py` attacks the first interior degree (2,2,2) by partitioning off-diagonal magnitudes into 1 versus 2+x, x>=0, and looking for a sign-definite maximal minor of the joint lowering matrix. A positive-coefficient determinant with positive constant would certify a uniform parameter cell; failure of that sign test would be inconclusive, not a counterexample. Its scope is only one degree, not all heights. The saved output records the exercised cell and outcome.
   112	
   113	No all-height reduction of interior degrees was found. The standard invariant-form route cannot simply be applied to the original nonsymmetrizable A. Even the coefficient-one comparison breaks at coefficient two: altered i-row Serre relations and i-lowerings can then matter. Finite exact agreement, modular agreement, and the known symmetrizable theorem do not close that gap.
   114	
   115	### Reproduction
   116	
   117	From this directory, the core computations need only Python 3.14.3 and the standard library, one process each:
   118	
   119	```sh
   120	python3 work/compute.py --height 10 --prime 1000003 --output evidence/modp-height10
   121	python3 work/compute.py --height 10 --output evidence/rational-height10
   122	python3 work/check_certificate.py evidence/rational-height10/certificate.json.gz --height 10 --matrices A3_control affine_A2_control one_asymmetric_edge oriented_double_cycle larger_asymmetric_cycle --output evidence/rational-height10/independent-check.json --negative-controls
   123	python3 work/compute.py --height 12 --prime 1000003 --matrices one_asymmetric_edge --output evidence/modp-height12
   124	python3 work/compute.py --height 12 --matrices one_asymmetric_edge --output evidence/rational-height12
   125	python3 work/check_certificate.py evidence/rational-height12/certificate.json.gz --height 12 --matrices one_asymmetric_edge --output evidence/rational-height12/independent-check.json --negative-controls
   126	```
   127	
   128	The separate symbolic experiment uses an isolated uv environment, not a global installation:
   129	
   130	```sh
   131	env UV_CACHE_DIR=/tmp/kac-serre-uv-cache OPENBLAS_NUM_THREADS=1 OMP_NUM_THREADS=1 uv run --no-project --with sympy --with python-flint python work/interior_minor.py --mask 0 --output evidence/symbolic-222
   132	```
   133	
   134	No more than four computation processes were run concurrently. No system package installation, live infrastructure change, or Git publication occurred. Finite certificates are compressed to keep the target small.
