evidence/descent-audit.md:49:The book's full-column-rank matrix `C` makes the simple roots linearly independent as functionals on `h`. Thus distinct root-lattice degrees have distinct `h`-weights. Every ideal is `h`-stable, so it splits into homogeneous components: on the finite set of weights appearing in any particular vector, polynomial projections in a suitable `ad(h)` extract those components. This is where the full realization and characteristic zero matter. Using only the rows of a singular `A` to identify distinct weights would leave a gap in this argument.
