README.md:23:Starting from the preliminary contragredient Lie algebra with Chevalley/Cartan relations, there are two quotients: the explicit Serre quotient S(A), and the quotient g(A) by the unique maximal ideal meeting the Cartan subalgebra trivially. The conjecture asserts that these coincide for every A. They are known to coincide for symmetrizable A. Some sources call S(A) itself “the Kac–Moody algebra”; this dossier always distinguishes the two constructions.
README.md:31:**English:** “Conjecture 1. For every generalized Cartan matrix A, the Serre relations are defining relations of the Kac–Moody algebra g(A).” Here g(A) is the book's maximal-Cartan-disjoint-ideal quotient, defined immediately before the conjecture; “Serre relations” includes its displayed Chevalley/Cartan relations (1) and the positive/negative relations (2). See excerpt lines 12–34.
README.md:37:- **Most explicit modern statement opened:** Robert Theodore Williams Jr., *Commutator Formulas in Groups of Kac-Moody Type*, thesis, August 2022, DOI [10.18130/t9v1-vz61](https://doi.org/10.18130/t9v1-vz61), printed p.49 / PDF p.55, after Definition 6.1.5: “They coincide in (at least) the case that A is a symmetrizable matrix … but it is not known if they always coincide or if there is a GCM A for which they do not.” The preceding text explicitly identifies the two quotients. Full PDF opened and saved as `sources/williams-thesis-2022.pdf`; text lines 2079–2098.
