   111	`work/interior_minor.py` attacks the first interior degree (2,2,2) by partitioning off-diagonal magnitudes into 1 versus 2+x, x>=0, and looking for a sign-definite maximal minor of the joint lowering matrix. A positive-coefficient determinant with positive constant would certify a uniform parameter cell; failure of that sign test would be inconclusive, not a counterexample. Its scope is only one degree, not all heights. The saved output records the exercised cell and outcome.
   112	
   113	No all-height reduction of interior degrees was found. The standard invariant-form route cannot simply be applied to the original nonsymmetrizable A. Even the coefficient-one comparison breaks at coefficient two: altered i-row Serre relations and i-lowerings can then matter. Finite exact agreement, modular agreement, and the known symmetrizable theorem do not close that gap.
   114	
   115	### Reproduction
   116	
   117	From this directory, the core computations need only Python 3.14.3 and the standard library, one process each:
   118	
   119	```sh
   120	python3 work/compute.py --height 10 --prime 1000003 --output evidence/modp-height10
   121	python3 work/compute.py --height 10 --output evidence/rational-height10
   122	python3 work/check_certificate.py evidence/rational-height10/certificate.json.gz --height 10 --matrices A3_control affine_A2_control one_asymmetric_edge oriented_double_cycle larger_asymmetric_cycle --output evidence/rational-height10/independent-check.json --negative-controls
   123	python3 work/compute.py --height 12 --prime 1000003 --matrices one_asymmetric_edge --output evidence/modp-height12
   124	python3 work/compute.py --height 12 --matrices one_asymmetric_edge --output evidence/rational-height12
   125	python3 work/check_certificate.py evidence/rational-height12/certificate.json.gz --height 12 --matrices one_asymmetric_edge --output evidence/rational-height12/independent-check.json --negative-controls
   126	```
