**READY** for the replacement checker and Section 5. No new correctness errors requiring fixes were found. Height-12 acceptance remains pending.

- **Scope binding closes the omitted-matrix loophole.** [Scope checks](/Users/jinleic/jinleic-workspace/ai4s/kac-moody-serre-relations/work/check_certificate.py:178), lines 178–198, require the requested height, exact matrix-name set, fixed entries, and complete ordered degree list. Omitting, substituting, or relabeling a matrix cannot pass under the prescribed arguments. The CLI permits other explicitly requested scopes and `--spec` values; their PASS receipts must be distinguished using the recorded height, names, and specification hash.

- **Exact arithmetic and degree coverage are sound.** [Basis construction and elimination](/Users/jinleic/jinleic-workspace/ai4s/kac-moody-serre-relations/work/check_certificate.py:64) use rational `Fraction` arithmetic. Exhaustive suffix-Lyndon enumeration, Witt counts, monic triangularity, and exact record-list comparison cover every nonzero free-Lie component through the requested height. Zero-dimensional degrees require no certificate rows.

